---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Base path="/privacy" title="Privacy" description="What this website does and does not collect: consent-gated analytics, embedded dashboards and booking a call.">
  <article class="plain">
    <h1>What this site does with your data</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated 14 November 2026. This is a plain-language description of how the site works, not legal advice.</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>This is the personal website of Arnav Patnaik, {site.location}. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The site is a set of static pages. It has no accounts, no sign-in, no forms that store your details and no advertising.</li>
      <li>Optional analytics runs <strong>only if you accept it</strong>. If you decline, nothing is loaded.</li>
      <li>Some features load content from third parties (for example Calendly or Microsoft Power BI), and only after you choose to open them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="analytics">Analytics (optional)</h2>
    <p>If you choose <em>Accept analytics</em>, the site uses Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages are read. Google may set cookies and receive information such as the page visited, approximate location, and device and browser details, under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>. If you choose <em>Decline</em>, nothing is loaded and no analytics cookie is set. You can change your mind at any time with the button below.</p>
    <p><button type="button" class="btn" data-open-consent>Change my analytics choice</button></p>

    <h2>Booking a call and email</h2>
    <p>The "Let's work together" card can show a Calendly scheduling page. Nothing is requested from Calendly until you open the card. After that, Calendly handles what you enter there under its own <a href="https://calendly.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy notice<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>. If you prefer, you can write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> instead. Email is handled by your email provider and mine like any other email, and I use what you send only to reply to you.</p>

    <h2>Embedded dashboards</h2>
    <p>Some project pages can show public Power BI reports. Nothing is requested from Microsoft until you press "Load the interactive dashboard". After that, Microsoft may receive your IP address and set its own cookies under <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft's privacy statement<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>. You can avoid this by not pressing the button.</p>

    <h2>Stored in your browser</h2>
    <p>The site stores a single setting in your browser, your analytics choice, so that it does not ask you again. You can clear it in your browser settings at any time.</p>

    <h2>Third-party services and links</h2>
    <p>This site links to other services such as GitHub, LinkedIn, ResearchGate, conference sites and dashboards. They are run by other parties with their own privacy practices, and I am not responsible for them.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask what personal data I hold about you, and ask for it to be corrected or deleted, by emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. If you are in the EU you can also contact your data protection authority; in Belgium that is the Data Protection Authority (APD/GBA).</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If the way the site handles data changes, this page is updated and the date above changes. By continuing to use the site you accept the version that is current at the time.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
